SUMMARY:Readers Circle Storytime
DESCRIPTION:Designed to help encourage children's literacy by focusing on 
 reading comprehension skills.\n\nHosted by TAG (Teen Advisory Group). For 
 Children in 1st and 2nd grades. Registration not required.\n\nWe have a 
 group of teens\, ages 12 - 18\, who would like to share the reading 
 experience with children in 1st and 2nd grades. Every other Saturday from 
 10:30 - 11:15 a.m.\, a teen volunteer will read aloud from age-appropriate 
 books and help children identify key parts of the story. Games to enhance 
 learning will be included. One-on-one help for 3rd and 4th graders is 
 available upon request.\n\nBooks from which selections will be taken 
 include Splat the Cat by Rob Scotton\, Elephant and Piggie by Mo Willems\, 
 Amelia Bedelia by Peggy Parish and Fancy Nancy by Jane O'Connor.
LOCATION:Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Michelle Desranleau":MAILTO:michelle@miltonlibraryvt.org
CATEGORIES:Children's Programs
UID:LibCal-20373-17494224
URL:https://miltonlibraryvt.libcal.com/event/17494224
END:VEVENT
