SUMMARY:Herbs for Winter Health Support
DESCRIPTION:Do you wonder what to do to ‘cure a cold’? Ward off the 
 latest flus? What is the best approach for coughs\, sore throats and head 
 congestion? Or seasonal depression? Better yet\, what to do to prevent the 
 malady’s that often come with the long Vermont winters. In this hands-on 
 class\, Rosemary Gladstar focus will be on prevention\,  remedies for 
 wellness\, and what to stock in a winter pantry to be prepared for winter 
 health  concerns.  Rosemary will also share her favorite remedies and 
 recipes including fire cider\, elderberry syrup\, echinacea tincture\, and 
 favorite ways to administer herbs.  Registration required.  \n\nPhoto 
 credit:  Rosemary Gladstar
LOCATION:Community Room
ORGANIZER;CN="MaryBeth Peterson":MAILTO:marybeth@miltonlibraryvt.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs
UID:LibCal-20373-17450398
URL:https://miltonlibraryvt.libcal.com/event/17450398
