BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261112T230000Z
DTEND:20261113T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20261112T000000Z
SUMMARY:Hands-On Nutrition & Charcuterie Board Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Discover the essentials of protein and nutrition with Leslie 
 Piela from Lakelife Nutrition in this engaging hands-on class. You'll learn 
 how much protein your body needs to prevent muscle loss while enjoying 
 delicious samples of hummus and protein-packed snacks. Plus\, you'll create 
 your own mini charcuterie board.  A variety of teas will be available to 
 sample. Registration is required.\n
LOCATION:Community Room
ORGANIZER;CN="Michelle Desranleau":MAILTO:michelle@miltonlibraryvt.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs
UID:LibCal-20373-17854583
URL:https://miltonlibraryvt.libcal.com/event/17854583
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261114T153000Z
DTEND:20261114T163000Z
DTSTAMP:20261114T000000Z
SUMMARY:Freestyle Craft Club:  Tiny Worlds
DESCRIPTION:Drop in for our monthly crafting sessions with Kristi Dickinson 
 designed for ages 4 to 8. Each month features a new theme\, allowing kids 
 to explore\, create\, and craft. Supplies are provided.  Enjoy a storytime 
 led by a special guest from our Reader's Circle. \n\n10/3:  Monster Lab - 
 build a monster and give your creature a name and a unique superpower. In 
 addition\, design a habitat\, pet\, vehicle\, or special outfit for your 
 monster.  Plus\, partner up\, start a creation\, and trade halfway through 
 to finish each other's monsters.  \n\n11/14:  Tiny Worlds - build a 
 miniature dwelling\, craft an island\, craft a miniature creature while 
 another builds its home\n\n12/5:  The Spirit of Giving - make a handmade 
 gift for someone special\, create something throughtful for a community 
 hero or neighbor\, work together to create a special project to give to the 
 library\n\n1/2:  Robot Workshop - build a bot\, create a robotic pet to 
 keep your robot company\, ask a crafter what task they wish a robot could 
 do\, then design one for them\n\n2/6:  Outer Space - make something 
 mysterious you might discover on a distant planet\, build a rocket\, 
 shuttle\, or vehicle capable of deep-space travel\, build a planet\n\n3/6:  
 Rainbows & Color - craft something that incorporates every color of the 
 rainbow\, reimagine an everyday item that's usually dull using vibrant 
 colors instead\, pick 3 specific colors for your partner to use for their 
 design\n\n
LOCATION:Community Room
ORGANIZER;CN="Lorraine Kelm":MAILTO:lorraine@miltonlibraryvt.org
CATEGORIES:Children's Programs
UID:LibCal-20373-17729969
URL:https://miltonlibraryvt.libcal.com/event/17729969
END:VEVENT
